Source: librknnrt
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-toolkit2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)

Package: librknnrt
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rockchip RKNN runtime for the NPU
 librknnrt is the userspace runtime for the Rockchip NPU: it loads an .rknn
 model and runs inference on the RKNPU cores through the kernel's RKNPU
 driver. It is a closed-source prebuilt library, so there is nothing here to
 build from source.
 .
 The runtime checks the driver it finds and will refuse to run against one it
 considers too old, so this package and the kernel belong to the same
 Rockchip baseline. Version 2.3.2 is the one that ships with rkr7.
 .
 The library's SONAME carries no version, which is why the bare
 librknnrt.so symlink is in this package and not in librknnrt-dev: it is
 the link the dynamic loader follows, not just the one the linker needs.

Package: librknnrt-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: librknnrt (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rockchip RKNN runtime -- development headers
 rknn_api.h, rknn_matmul_api.h and rknn_custom_op.h, the headers for
 building against librknnrt.
 .
 The library this builds against has an unversioned SONAME, so the .so
 symlink a linker resolves is the same one the loader needs at run time and
 lives in librknnrt. This package is headers only.

Package: rknn-server
Section: misc
Architecture: arm64
Depends: librknnrt (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rockchip RKNN debug server
 rknn_server runs on the board and lets rknn-toolkit2 on a host machine
 drive inference over a connection, which is how a model is checked against
 real hardware before it is deployed. It is a development aid and is in its
 own package so that installing the runtime does not start a daemon.
